---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Washy washy — privacy policy"
  description="No account, cookies, analytics or tracking. An uploaded config or chart edit stays in your own browser and is never sent anywhere."
>
  <h1 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-ink sm:text-3xl">Privacy policy</h1>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-base text-body">
    <p>
      Washy washy has no account, no cookies, no analytics and no tracking scripts of any kind.
      There is nothing here watching what you do on the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Uploading your own config, or editing the chart or machine settings, saves that data only in
      your own browser's storage (<code class="text-sm text-ink">localStorage</code>). It never
      leaves your device — not to a server, not to us, not to anyone. Clearing your browser's site
      data for washy washy removes it completely.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site itself is static — plain files with no backend — served by{" "}
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/cloudflare-workers/"
        class="underline decoration-hairline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-text hover:decoration-accent"
      >
        Cloudflare Workers
      </a>. Like any web host, Cloudflare's own infrastructure sees the ordinary HTTP request
      metadata involved in serving a page — your IP address, browser, the page requested — the
      same as any site you visit. Washy washy itself has no access to that, and doesn't ask
      Cloudflare or anyone else for it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
